  "slug": "salmon-crepes-with-yogurt-sauce",
  "title": "Salmon Crêpes with Yogurt Sauce",
  "blurb": "Light crêpes filled with flaked salmon and served with a tangy yogurt dressing",
  "steps": [
    "Whisk the flour, salt, baking soda and cold water together until smooth, then stir in half the canola oil.",
    "Heat a non-stick frying pan over medium heat and cook thin crêpes using a small ladleful of batter for each, about one minute per side until lightly golden.",
    "Meanwhile, place the salmon in a shallow pan with enough water to cover and simmer gently for 8 minutes until cooked through.",
    "Drain the salmon and flake it into chunks with a fork, discarding any bones.",
    "Mix the Greek yogurt with lemon juice and chopped dill to make a sauce.",
    "Fill each crêpe with flaked salmon, fold into quarters, and serve with the yogurt sauce on the side."
